    "id": "scale-loop",
    "caption": "Scale on unmet demand: queue depth drives new replicas, but each one pays a multi-minute cold start before it can serve, so warm capacity and admission control cover the gap.",
    "alt": "Requests arrive at an admission control layer that rejects excess load with HTTP 429. Admitted requests queue at the engine replicas. Prometheus scrapes queue depth, and KEDA scales the deployment when waiting requests exceed a threshold. A new replica goes through node provisioning, image pull, weight loading and warm-up before becoming ready.",
